WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.930
It's Saturday, November 28, and this is the Transhuman Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.030
Here's your day in transhumanism, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.180
Mind readers! In an early trial,

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:21.480
a Shanghai brain implant gave a woman with ALS her voice back.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:27.850
And a smart ring sensed stress from fingertip sweat, 92% right, in a tiny test.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.090
Tencent's AI designed a drug that beat Wegovy's ingredient in mice,

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:37.410
at a tenth the dose.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.290
South Carolina scientists gave an AI a mock stroke.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:45.470
Its word mix-ups echoed real stroke survivors'.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.090
And in a UK first,

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:51.120
an AI agent paid for nine pizzas straight from a bank account.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.060
Peter Gabriel's idea: if we can't beat AI, join it,

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:58.970
by uploading superintelligence into our brains.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.010
On to longevity.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:06.390
A quick tablet test plus a blood test could spare most memory patients a brain scan.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.660
In killifish, males that fathered most when young lived longest,

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:13.810
upending 'live fast, die young'.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.430
Meanwhile, in old mice, one way of boosting NAD+,

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.280
a molecule longevity pills chase, thinned their bones.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:23.600
Closer to home,

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:29.250
72% of older Australians changed doctors when they moved into nursing homes.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.580
Wellbeing now. Pooling six small trials,

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:36.900
psilocybin therapy nearly tripled the odds of staying off alcohol.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.640
And Kyoto scientists may have found the brain's dream-sleep switch,

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:43.990
a clue to spotting Parkinson's early.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.990
Now, the catch.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:52.310
Australian researchers say AI studies linking fingerprints to blood type used mislabelled data.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.110
And Australia passed a law making apps and

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:57.920
AI chatbots protect users from serious harm.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.250
On the frontier, the plastic in comic-book bags,

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:08.760
stacked hundreds deep, could insulate moon bases.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:11.900
A Georgia Tech robot with soft silicone t

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.970
humbs grasped 23 of 25 blueberry clusters.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:20.340
And a German start-up is piloting chips that run AI maths on light,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:21.320
to save power.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.280
Implants that speak for us,

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.970
rings that feel our stress. Here's to the mind readers!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.510
Zoom out, and the line only goes up.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.440
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.170
You've been watching the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.140
Live long. See you tomorrow.
